<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Aleg</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Aleg is a town in south-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mauritania">Mauritania</a> and the capital of the Brakna region, on the road between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nouakchott">Nouakchott</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/senegal-river">Senegal River</a> valley, beside a seasonal lake. It lies in the former lands of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emirate">Emirate</a> of Brakna, whose <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emir">emirs</a> dominated the area until French colonial rule in the early 20th century.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/aleg.jpg" alt="Aleg" width="320" height="211" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Toksave · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Aleg_mauritania.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
